{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789463658,"nonce":"xOiozwHExrh1KgrkIwsWl/y1MQA=","title":"wren_lift's cycle cannot place a stack of the core's making","message":"wren_lift's collection scans stacks itself (`conservative_stack_ranges`): for each thread it walks the chain of its own krio fibers from the current one by `caller_sp`, and takes whatever the chain ends on as the thread's own stack up to its top. A fiber the core made, a Haxe task, is not among its fibers, so a thread inside one is scanned as (probe on the fiber's stack, thread's top), a range spanning whatever lies between two mappings; and a Haxe task suspended with Wren frames on its stack is not scanned at all. Under the one world (df96108) this is reached by a Haxe task calling Wren code that parks: `park_drive` then leaves the view running rather than mark it safe with a stack the collector cannot place, so a Wren cycle on another thread waits for that thread's next Wren poll, and a Wren value held only by the suspended task's Wren frames is not a root of that cycle. Before the one world the same held whenever a Haxe task called Wren while a Wren cycle ran.\n\nTwo ways out:\n- The seam tells wren_lift the host's stacks: a slot handing over every stack the core's registry holds with where each is suspended, and the current thread's own stack's suspended point when it is inside a foreign fiber. wren_lift then scans foreign stacks from their suspended point as it scans its own fibers.\n- One collector: the core's cycle marks Wren objects too. The anchor retains every pin because the core cannot see wren_lift's roots; a slot handing those over (the same gathering wren_lift's cycle does) would let the core's precise trace and its conservative scan of every registered stack decide what is dead, and wren_lift's own cycle would go under the adapter. The stack question then disappears with the second collector.\n\nThe second is the direction; the first is the smaller change. `tests/world.rs` exercises Wren tasks calling Haxe, not Haxe tasks calling Wren that park.","files":null}]}